      "side": 1,
      "message": "A problem with this function is that it\u0027s generic with respect to fan_table but it keeps these values for a particular fan_table. The logic makes sense only if \u003cfan_table\u003e points to the same table. If we assume there is only one fan table, why don\u0027t you make the function internally reference it?\n\nThe same problem applies to fan_index. For example, you can infer fan_stopped from fan_get_rpm_target(FAN_CH(fan_index)) to get rid of the assumption that fan_index is always the same.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 81,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 83,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "552be44e86a5d00ecf5232641a4936c399c769ad",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
